{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on eb1ed32c (evidence-rules preparation: the room-service key\nmark, rotation, and wrong-source enforcement). All three points are\napproved as you state them, with the amendments below.\n\nA. Approved. The Rules singleton owns at most one roomService pair\n{checker member, key}, published only by an active admin through the\nnative publish path; null withdraws it; new genesis is unmarked; the\nlast-mark-change position is native-selected and scoped to the exact\nRules incarnation; no self-hash in effects. Publish observes that the\nmember is an active checker member and refuses otherwise. The key is\nproven at every use (admission and result judgment), not atomically at\nmarking. No additional native owner or exchange for marking-time proof.\n\nB. Approved. Admission freezes the marked member, key and generation\nwith the exact job, tree, configuration, source and stage. After\nDestination observes a rotation, neither key completes that fence; a\nnew explicitly requested job is needed; no automatic restart, re-sign,\nreuse or reclassification; old accepted results stay historical; reuse\nchecks today's eligible signer; audits run fresh. Timing is the bounded\nnative observation order. No Destination-local fence or handshake, and\nno immediate global revocation at the Rules commit. Amendment: the\nrefusal keeps the word wrong-source and records the frozen generation\nand the observed generation in its data, so the record shows why.\n\nC. Approved. Destination's refusal to count a wrong-source result is\nthe enforcement for the commissioned witness. The lane may retain an\nordinarily member-authorized result; Destination refuses to count it,\nand the refusal is recorded where the lane's readers see it. No\nactor-key DSL operand, no new native guard or exchange now. Revisit\nonly if the exit test shows people misled by a retained result.\n\nTwo conditions. The slice's head updates the design note's sentence\n\"Which scope holds the mark, and how a rotation ... is still open\" to\nstate this disposition, so the note's status matches main\n(notes/2026-10-16-evidence-rules-design.md:109-112). The marked key is\nthe key J3's service signs with outside the container; the preparation\nmemo names that binding.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}